0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 46.00 240.00 Td ("Before we crunch numbers, let's define our tools.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 46.00 229.50 Td (A system of linear equations can be stripped of its variable letters and stored as an augmented matrix.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 46.00 219.00 Td (The left side holds the coefficients of x, y, and z, separated by a line from the constants on the right.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 46.00 208.50 Td (Our goal is to reach Row Echelon Form--an upper-triangular pattern with zeros below the diagonal.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 46.00 198.00 Td (To get there, we use three elementary row operations: swapping rows, scaling a row by a non-zero constant, or adding a multiple of one row to another.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 46.00 187.50 Td (The leading non-zero number in each row is called a pivot.") Tj ET
