BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 353.50 Td (  Column 2 has -3 in row 2 and 1 in row 3. Swapping avoids introducing fractions!) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 344.00 Td (  Smooth 3D card-flip swap \(191.5s-194.6s\): Row 2 = [0, 1, -2 | -4], Row 3 = [0, -3, -1 | -9].) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 334.50 Td (  Pivot 2 = 1 at position \(2, 2\).) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 325.00 Td () Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 315.50 Td (STEP 4D: Eliminate y from Row 3 \(R3 -> R3 + 3*R2\)  [3:19 - 3:41]) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 306.00 Td (  Target = -3 at \(3,2\).) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 296.50 Td (  Calculation:  [0, -3, -1 | -9] + 3*[0, 1, -2 | -4] = [0+0, -3+3, -1-6 | -9-12] = [0, 0, -7 | -21]) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 287.00 Td (  Matrix M_REF: Row 3 becomes [0, 0, -7 | -21].) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 277.50 Td (  Staircase highlighted: Pivots = 1, 1, -7. All entries below pivots are zero. REF ACHIEVED!) Tj ET
0.700 0.200 0.100 rg
BT /F2 8 Tf 46.00 220.00 Td (EXACT SPOKEN NARRATION SCRIPT \(Steps 4A - 4D\):) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 208.00 Td ("Let's work through our system step-by-step. Our first pivot is the one in the top-left corner.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 198.50 Td (To eliminate the two beneath it in Row 2, we subtract two times Row 1 from Row 2.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 189.00 Td (Two minus two is zero; negative one minus two is negative three; one minus two is negative one; and three minus twelve gives negative nine.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 179.50 Td (Our first zero is locked in.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 170.00 Td (Next, to eliminate the one in Row 3, we subtract Row 1 from Row 3.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 160.50 Td (One minus one is zero; two minus one is one; negative one minus one is negative two; and two minus six gives negative four.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 151.00 Td (Column one now has zeros everywhere below the first pivot.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 141.50 Td (Now look at column two. Row 2 has negative three, but Row 3 has a clean one.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 132.00 Td (Instead of dividing by negative three and creating awkward fractions, we swap Row 2 and Row 3. Now our second pivot is a simple one.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 122.50 Td (To eliminate the negative three now sitting in Row 3, we add three times Row 2 to Row 3.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 113.00 Td (Zero plus zero is zero; negative three plus three is zero; negative one plus negative six is negative seven; and negative nine plus negative twelve is negative twenty-one.) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.200 rg
BT /F3 7 Tf 46.00 103.50 Td (Look at that: we have reached Row Echelon Form!") Tj ET
