BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 498.00 Td (1. Determinant Verification: det\(A\) = 1*\(-1*-1 - 1*2\) - 1*\(2*-1 - 1*1\) + 1*\(2*2 - -1*1\) = 1*\(-1\) - 1*\(-3\) + 1*\(5\) = 7 != 0.) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 488.00 Td (   Since det\(A\) = 7 != 0, matrix A is invertible, has full rank 3, and guarantees a unique intersection point in R^3.) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 478.00 Td (2. REF Determinant Consistency: In echelon form, product of diagonal elements is 1 * 1 * \(-7\) = -7.) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 468.00 Td (   Accounting for exactly one row swap \(R2 <-> R3\) which multiplies det by \(-1\): det\(A\) = -1 * \(-7\) = 7 \(Consistent\).) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 458.00 Td (3. Solution Set Invariance: Elementary row operations correspond to multiplication by invertible elementary matrices) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.150 rg
BT /F5 7 Tf 46.00 448.00 Td (   E1, E2, P23, E4. Since each elementary matrix is non-singular, Sol\(Ax = b\) = Sol\(Ux = b'\) is mathematically invariant.) Tj ET
